Why these and not others. Steam's `library_hero` has no title on it, and
its 3.1:1 shape keeps a third of itself in a square. Every square key art
the stores carry puts the title in its top quarter (Warzone, Fortnite, NBA
2K26) or its lower middle (Black Ops 7, Apex Legends), where the chips or
the name cover it, so each crop above is the one that keeps the title whole
in the band the banners leave. Fortnite's is the Fortnite OG key art, not
the season's: the season's square ("Fortnitemares") does not say
"Fortnite", and the Battle Royale square puts the word under the chips.
Black Ops 7's says "Cross-Gen Bundle" under the title because the PlayStation
Store sells the game as that bundle; Steam has no square art for it.

**Not given a panel picture (they draw their tall one):** NBA 2K27 (the
pack whose id is still `nba-2k26`, D475). Its predecessor's square key art
put the title in the top fifth, under the chips; 2K27's tall cover is drawn
in the panel instead. Every pack whose game has
no pictures at all (the list below) also has no panel picture.

